      <main id="main-content">
        <section class="lesson" id="mental-model">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 01</p>
          <h2>Think in systems, not markers.</h2>
          <p class="lede">MapLibre becomes predictable when you use one mental model: <strong>data → source → layer → interaction</strong>.</p>
          <div class="plain"><strong>In plain words</strong>Your information lives somewhere. MapLibre reads it as a source. Layers decide what it looks like. Interactions decide what happens when people use it.</div>
          <figure class="diagram">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 900 270" role="img" aria-labelledby="d1t d1d">
              <title id="d1t">MapLibre mental model</title>
              <desc id="d1d">Four connected boxes show data flowing to source, layer, then interaction.</desc>
              <defs><marker id="arr1" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="8" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1.6"/></marker></defs>
              <g class="svg-text" font-size="18" font-weight="700">
                <rect class="svg-soft" x="40" y="70" width="170" height="110" rx="6"/><text x="125" y="118" text-anchor="middle">DATA</text><text class="svg-muted" x="125" y="148" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="400">stops · days · hotels</text>
                <rect class="svg-panel" x="260" y="70" width="170" height="110" rx="6"/><text x="345" y="118" text-anchor="middle">SOURCE</text><text class="svg-muted" x="345" y="148" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="400">GeoJSON · DEM</text>
                <rect class="svg-panel" x="480" y="70" width="170" height="110" rx="6"/><text x="565" y="118" text-anchor="middle">LAYER</text><text class="svg-muted" x="565" y="148" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="400">line · symbol · fill</text>
                <rect class="svg-panel" x="700" y="70" width="160" height="110" rx="6"/><text x="780" y="118" text-anchor="middle">ACTION</text><text class="svg-muted" x="780" y="148" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="400">click · hover · focus</text>
              </g>
              <g fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arr1)"><path d="M210 125h42"/><path d="M430 125h42"/><path d="M650 125h42"/></g>
              <path class="svg-accent" d="M44 211H856" stroke-width="4"/><text class="svg-text" x="450" y="242" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13">ONE CANONICAL MODEL → MANY VISUAL TREATMENTS</text>
            </svg>
            <figcaption>Design-system translation: source = data provider; layer = visual component; paint/layout = visual rules.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="callout"><b>Rule:</b> one source can power many layers. A stop source can render pins, labels, and selection halos without duplicating data.</div>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="structure">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 02</p><h2>Give every file one job.</h2>
          <div class="grid-2">
            <article class="card"><span class="tag">trip.js</span><h3>Content model</h3><p>Coordinates, day ranges, hotels, activities, drive-time text.</p></article>
            <article class="card"><span class="tag">map.js</span><h3>Map behavior</h3><p>MapLibre setup, sources, layers, camera, popups, state.</p></article>
            <article class="card"><span class="tag">styles.css</span><h3>Interface</h3><p>Sidebar, cards, typography, responsive layout, popup chrome.</p></article>
            <article class="card"><span class="tag">index.html</span><h3>Shell</h3><p>Semantic document structure and application mount points.</p></article>
          </div>
          <figure class="diagram">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 900 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="d2t d2d">
              <title id="d2t">Project architecture</title><desc id="d2d">A folder diagram showing index.html and src files connected by black lines.</desc>
              <g class="svg-text" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="17"><rect class="svg-panel" x="80" y="30" width="740" height="260" rx="8"/><text x="110" y="68" font-weight="800">maplibre-roadtrip-101/</text>
              <path d="M120 86v170M120 112h55M120 158h55M120 204h55M120 250h55" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="2"/>
              <text x="190" y="118">index.html</text><text x="190" y="164">README.md</text><text x="190" y="210">src/</text><text x="250" y="238">trip.js · map.js · styles.css</text>
              <path class="svg-accent" d="M250 246h390" stroke-width="4"/><text class="svg-muted" x="650" y="251" font-size="13">content → renderer → UI</text></g>
            </svg><figcaption>Keeping content separate from rendering lets learners safely edit the trip before they understand every map layer.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="load">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 03</p><h2>Load the map with a small, legible constructor.</h2>
          <div class="plain"><strong>In plain words</strong>The constructor tells MapLibre where to draw, what style to use, and where the camera starts.</div>
          <pre><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><code>const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty',
  center: [-71.8, -43.5],
  zoom: 4.2,
  minZoom: 3,
  maxZoom: 14,
  renderWorldCopies: false,
});</code></pre>
          <p><code>center</code> uses <strong>[longitude, latitude]</strong>. If your point lands in the wrong country, check coordinate order first.</p>
          <h3>Keep the load callback boring</h3>
          <pre><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><code>map.on('load', () => {
  styleBasemap();
  addTerrainHillshade();
  addTerrainTexture();
  addTripSources();
  addTripLayers();
  addMapInteractions();
  fitTrip({ animate: false });
});</code></pre>
          <p>The callback orchestrates. Named functions do the work.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="basemap">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 04</p><h2>Art-direct the basemap.</h2>
          <p class="lede">For this trip, the basemap should support the itinerary—not compete with it.</p>
          <figure class="diagram">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 900 360" role="img" aria-labelledby="d3t d3d"><title id="d3t">Layer hierarchy before and after simplification</title><desc id="d3d">Two stacks compare a busy basemap with a simplified editorial map.</desc>
              <g class="svg-text" font-size="15"><text x="210" y="36" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="800">DEFAULT</text><text x="690" y="36" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="800">EDITORIAL</text>
                <g transform="translate(70 58)"><rect class="svg-soft" width="280" height="48"/><text x="140" y="30" text-anchor="middle">POIs + business labels</text><rect class="svg-panel" y="58" width="280" height="48"/><text x="140" y="88" text-anchor="middle">town labels</text><rect class="svg-soft" y="116" width="280" height="48"/><text x="140" y="146" text-anchor="middle">roads</text><rect class="svg-panel" y="174" width="280" height="48"/><text x="140" y="204" text-anchor="middle">terrain + water</text></g>
                <g transform="translate(550 58)"><rect class="svg-highlight" width="280" height="48"/><text x="140" y="30" text-anchor="middle">trip stops + day labels</text><rect class="svg-panel" y="58" width="280" height="48"/><text x="140" y="88" text-anchor="middle">a few context places</text><rect class="svg-soft" y="116" width="280" height="48"/><text x="140" y="146" text-anchor="middle">quiet roads</text><rect class="svg-panel" y="174" width="280" height="48"/><text x="140" y="204" text-anchor="middle">terrain + water</text></g>
                <path d="M365 170h160" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M510 158l15 12-15 12" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="2"/>
                <text class="svg-muted" x="450" y="324" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13">REMOVE NOISE → ADD BACK ONLY TASK-RELEVANT CONTEXT</text></g>
            </svg><figcaption>Color is reserved for the information that moves the story forward.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <pre><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><code>for (const layer of map.getStyle().layers ?? []) {
  if (layer.type === 'symbol') {
    map.setLayoutProperty(layer.id, 'visibility', 'none');
  }
}</code></pre>
          <div class="callout"><b>Prototype:</b> runtime restyling is fast. <b>Production:</b> own and version your style JSON once the visual direction is stable.</div>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="terrain">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 05</p><h2>Terrain is a composition.</h2>
          <p>Hillshade needs elevation data, so first register a <code>raster-dem</code> source. Then add a <code>hillshade</code> layer.</p>
          <pre><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><code>map.addSource('terrain-dem', {
  type: 'raster-dem',
  url: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/terrain-tiles/tiles.json',
  tileSize: 256,
});</code></pre>
          <figure class="diagram">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 900 420" role="img" aria-labelledby="d4t d4d"><title id="d4t">Terrain layer stack</title><desc id="d4d">A vertical exploded stack shows basemap, hillshade, hatch texture, roads, and route.</desc>
              <g class="svg-text" font-size="16" font-weight="700"><g transform="translate(145 300)"><rect class="svg-panel" width="610" height="58" rx="4"/><text x="305" y="35" text-anchor="middle">BASEMAP</text></g><g transform="translate(175 235)"><rect class="svg-soft" width="550" height="52" rx="4"/><text x="275" y="32" text-anchor="middle">HILLSHADE</text></g><g transform="translate(205 176)"><rect class="svg-panel" width="490" height="46" rx="4"/><path d="M18 36l30-30M48 40L78 10M98 40l30-30M148 40l30-30M198 40l30-30M248 40l30-30M298 40l30-30M348 40l30-30M398 40l30-30" stroke="var(--soft-line)"/><text x="245" y="28" text-anchor="middle">HATCH TEXTURE</text></g><g transform="translate(245 120)"><rect class="svg-soft" width="410" height="42" rx="4"/><text x="205" y="27" text-anchor="middle">ROADS</text></g><g transform="translate(300 70)"><rect class="svg-highlight" width="300" height="38" rx="4"/><text x="150" y="25" text-anchor="middle">TRIP ROUTE</text></g></g>
            </svg><figcaption>There is no single “patterned hillshade” property. The visual is built from several simple layers.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="plain"><strong>In plain words</strong>Hillshade makes the land feel dimensional. A transparent pattern adds a print-like texture. They are separate layers stacked together.</div>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="data">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 06</p><h2>Make the trip editable before making the map clever.</h2>
          <pre><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><code>{
  id: 'el-chalten',
  order: 7,
  name: 'El Chaltén',
  country: 'Argentina',
  coordinates: [-72.8863, -49.3315],
  dayRange: 'Days 8–9',
  days: 2,
  driveFromPrevious: '7h 30m',
  stay: 'Hiker lodge in town',
  plan: ['Fitz Roy viewpoints', 'Short hike', 'Bakery breakfast'],
}</code></pre>
          <p>This one object can feed the stop directory, popup, label, route, and selected state.</p>
          <div class="callout"><b>Design principle:</b> build one canonical itinerary model. Do not maintain separate map stops, sidebar stops, and popup stops.</div>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="sources">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 07</p><h2>Convert app data into map data.</h2>
          <p>MapLibre is happiest when geographic data arrives as GeoJSON.</p>
          <pre><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><code>export function buildStopsGeoJSON() {
  return {
    type: 'FeatureCollection',
    features: stops.map((stop) => ({
      type: 'Feature',
      id: stop.order,
      properties: {
        id: stop.id,
        name: stop.name,
        dayRange: stop.dayRange,
      },
      geometry: {
        type: 'Point',
        coordinates: stop.coordinates,
      },
    })),
  };
}</code></pre>
          <div class="plain"><strong>In plain words</strong>Your rich JavaScript object can stay rich. Copy only the fields the map needs into GeoJSON.</div>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="route">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 08</p><h2>Build the route from visual primitives.</h2>
          <p>The route is one source rendered twice: a pale casing underneath and a colored line above.</p>
          <figure class="diagram">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 900 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="d5t d5d"><title id="d5t">Schematic roadtrip route</title><desc id="d5d">A vertical route diagram from Santiago to Torres del Paine with ten stops.</desc>
              <path d="M460 40C410 84 505 112 442 154S500 226 444 290" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="14" stroke-linecap="round" opacity=".18"/>
              <path d="M460 40C410 84 505 112 442 154S500 226 444 290" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              <g fill="var(--panel)" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="460" cy="40" r="9"/><circle cx="435" cy="74" r="8"/><circle cx="454" cy="103" r="8"/><circle cx="474" cy="130" r="8"/><circle cx="442" cy="154" r="8"/><circle cx="430" cy="187" r="8"/><circle cx="463" cy="216" r="8"/><circle cx="475" cy="244" r="8"/><circle cx="456" cy="268" r="8"/><circle cx="444" cy="290" r="9"/></g>
              <g class="svg-text" font-size="13"><text x="495" y="45">Santiago</text><text x="495" y="218">El Chaltén</text><text x="495" y="296">Torres del Paine</text><text class="svg-muted" x="110" y="168">schematic line for learning</text><path d="M270 164h135" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1.5"/></g>
            </svg><figcaption>The tutorial connects stops directly. Replace the geometry with routing output when you are ready for real roads.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <pre><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><code>map.addLayer({
  id: 'trip-route-line',
  type: 'line',
  source: 'trip-route',
  paint: {
    'line-width': ['interpolate', ['linear'], ['zoom'], 3, 2.5, 8, 5],
    'line-gradient': [
      'interpolate', ['linear'], ['line-progress'],
      0, MAP_TOKENS.routeStart,
      1, MAP_TOKENS.routeEnd,
    ],
  },
});</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="labels">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 09</p><h2>Use labels editorially.</h2>
          <p>Stop labels combine place and schedule:</p>
          <pre><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><code>'text-field': [
  'concat',
  ['get', 'name'],
  '\n',
  ['get', 'dayRange'],
]</code></pre>
          <p>Context labels should be quieter, fewer, and smaller. The map is not obligated to display every label available in the basemap.</p>
          <div class="callout"><b>Information-design question:</b> does this label help a roadtrip buddy understand the trip? If not, remove it.</div>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="state">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 10</p><h2>Separate facts from temporary UI state.</h2>
          <figure class="diagram">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 900 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="d6t d6d"><title id="d6t">Persistent data versus temporary state</title><desc id="d6d">Two columns separate itinerary facts from selection and hover state.</desc>
              <g class="svg-text" font-size="16"><rect class="svg-panel" x="70" y="50" width="340" height="190" rx="6"/><text x="240" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="800">PERSISTENT FACTS</text><text x="110" y="130">• name</text><text x="110" y="160">• coordinates</text><text x="110" y="190">• day range</text><text x="110" y="220">• hotel</text>
              <rect class="svg-soft" x="490" y="50" width="340" height="190" rx="6"/><text x="660" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="800">TEMPORARY STATE</text><text x="530" y="130">• selected</text><text x="530" y="160">• hovered</text><text x="530" y="190">• focused</text><text x="530" y="220">• hidden</text><path class="svg-accent" d="M450 42v206" stroke-width="4"/></g>
            </svg><figcaption>Facts belong in data. Interaction state belongs in feature state or application state.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <pre><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><code>map.setFeatureState(
  { source: 'trip-stops', id: nextStop.order },
  { selected: true },
);</code></pre>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="camera">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 11</p><h2>Derive the camera from the trip.</h2>
          <p>Instead of hand-tuning one magic center and zoom, build bounds from the actual stops.</p>
          <pre><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><code>const bounds = new maplibregl.LngLatBounds();
for (const stop of stops) bounds.extend(stop.coordinates);

map.fitBounds(bounds, {
  padding: { top: 64, right: 64, bottom: 64, left: 96 },
  maxZoom: 5.4,
});</code></pre>
          <div class="plain"><strong>In plain words</strong>Add or remove stops and the overview camera still works because it is calculated from the data.</div>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="production">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 12</p><h2>Know the upgrade path.</h2>
          <figure class="diagram">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 900 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="d7t d7d"><title id="d7t">Prototype to production pipeline</title><desc id="d7d">Four stages show trip data flowing through routing, GeoJSON, and MapLibre.</desc><defs><marker id="arr2" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="8" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8" fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1.6"/></marker></defs>
              <g class="svg-text" font-size="15" font-weight="700"><rect class="svg-panel" x="45" y="70" width="165" height="88" rx="5"/><text x="127" y="106" text-anchor="middle">TRIP DATA</text><text class="svg-muted" x="127" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="400">stops + stays</text><rect class="svg-soft" x="270" y="70" width="165" height="88" rx="5"/><text x="352" y="106" text-anchor="middle">ROUTING</text><text class="svg-muted" x="352" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="400">roads + drive times</text><rect class="svg-panel" x="495" y="70" width="165" height="88" rx="5"/><text x="577" y="106" text-anchor="middle">GEOJSON</text><text class="svg-muted" x="577" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="400">stable interchange</text><rect class="svg-highlight" x="720" y="70" width="135" height="88" rx="5"/><text x="787" y="106" text-anchor="middle">MAPLIBRE</text><text class="svg-muted" x="787" y="132" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="400">render + interact</text></g>
              <g fill="none" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arr2)"><path d="M210 114h52"/><path d="M435 114h52"/><path d="M660 114h52"/></g>
            </svg><figcaption>Keep the layer design. Replace the underlying route geometry when you add a routing service.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="grid-2"><article class="card"><h3>Prototype</h3><p>Hosted basemap, demo terrain, schematic route, runtime restyling.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Production</h3><p>Owned style JSON, deliberate terrain provider, real routing, tested attribution and provider terms.</p></article></div>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="debug">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 13</p><h2>Debug in a fixed order.</h2>
          <details open><summary>The map is blank.</summary><p>Check that the map container has real width and height. A zero-height container renders nothing.</p></details>
          <details><summary>The marker is in the wrong country.</summary><p>GeoJSON uses <code>[longitude, latitude]</code>.</p></details>
          <details><summary>The icon is missing.</summary><p>Make sure <code>map.addImage()</code> runs before the symbol layer references that image ID.</p></details>
          <details><summary>The route gradient is missing.</summary><p>For a GeoJSON route that uses <code>line-progress</code>, enable <code>lineMetrics: true</code> on the source.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Labels disappear.</summary><p>That may be collision detection. Check text size, padding, overlap rules, and zoom ranges.</p></details>
          <details><summary>The overlay is under the basemap.</summary><p>Layer order is visual order. Use <code>map.addLayer(layer, beforeId)</code> or <code>map.moveLayer()</code>.</p></details>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson" id="themes">
          <p class="kicker">Lesson 14</p><h2>Choose the visual load that works for you.</h2>
          <p class="lede">All six themes preserve the same hierarchy. They change contrast, atmosphere, and surface treatment without changing lesson content.</p>
          <div class="theme-gallery" aria-label="Theme shortcuts">
            <button class="theme-chip" data-theme-choice="light"><strong>Light / Minimal</strong><small>White, black, and cool gray. Lowest decorative load.</small></button>
            <button class="theme-chip" data-theme-choice="night"><strong>Night Sky</strong><small>Cool dark outdoor palette with sparse star points.</small></button>
            <button class="theme-chip" data-theme-choice="note"><strong>Warm Note</strong><small>Pale yellow-beige field, white cards, warm brown rules.</small></button>
            <button class="theme-chip" data-theme-choice="signal"><strong>Signal Hacker</strong><small>Black field, bright blue signal, restrained lime highlights.</small></button>
            <button class="theme-chip" data-theme-choice="news"><strong>Grey Newspaper</strong><small>Monochrome, editorial, quiet, text-forward.</small></button>
            <button class="theme-chip" data-theme-choice="draft"><strong>Drafting Grid</strong><small>White container system over an architectural dot grid.</small></button>
