          <div class="callout"><b>Accessibility:</b> the theme switcher does not change content order, keyboard behavior, semantic headings, or diagram descriptions. Plain-language summaries can be hidden if they feel repetitive.</div>
        </section>

        <section class="lesson">
          <p class="kicker">Pocket reference</p><h2>The eight questions.</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>What is my canonical data?</li>
            <li>Which source owns the map version of that data?</li>
            <li>Which layers visualize that source?</li>
            <li>Which values are design tokens?</li>
            <li>Which values are feature properties?</li>
            <li>Which values are temporary state?</li>
            <li>What should the camera do after the user acts?</li>
            <li>Does this label help the task?</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="lede">If those answers are clear, most MapLibre code becomes much easier to reason about.</p>
        </section>
      </main>
